            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to General Noel J. Francisco (United States, amicus curiae), general Noel J. Francisco, amicus curiae for the United States, argued that Ohio\u2019s process was permissible before the 2002 clarification amendment, but that amendment made the rules clearer for two basic reasons."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Paul M. Smith (respondent)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "fef6eeae170a58e49c57f7fae6687524d3cc7e589fd23f8b3d1fcdd5892801ff",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-fef6eeae170a-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Paul M. Smith (respondent), paul M. Smith (respondent) contended that the Supplemental Process violates Section\u202f8 of the NVRA in two ways: it adds a failure\u2011to\u2011vote clause and it expands the list of permissible grounds beyond the four enumerated in the statute."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "fef6eeae170a58e49c57f7fae6687524d3cc7e589fd23f8b3d1fcdd5892801ff",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-fef6eeae170a-0003-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 67,
              "start": 67
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Heritage Reporting Corporation presented a fact that roughly 70\u202fpercent of people discard the notice, effectively \u201cthrowing it in the wastebasket.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "fef6eeae170a58e49c57f7fae6687524d3cc7e589fd23f8b3d1fcdd5892801ff",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-fef6eeae170a-0003-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 68,
              "start": 68
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Heritage Reporting Corporation noted that if a voter does not return the notice, the voter is placed on the inactive list."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "fef6eeae170a58e49c57f7fae6687524d3cc7e589fd23f8b3d1fcdd5892801ff",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-fef6eeae170a-0003-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 68,
              "start": 68
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor asked whether a voter who fails to return the notice would no longer receive election\u2011related mailings."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "fef6eeae170a58e49c57f7fae6687524d3cc7e589fd23f8b3d1fcdd5892801ff",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-fef6eeae170a-0003-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 72,
              "start": 72
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, justice Alito quoted the statutory language that \u201cno registrant may be removed solely by reason of failure to vote.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "fef6eeae170a58e49c57f7fae6687524d3cc7e589fd23f8b3d1fcdd5892801ff",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-fef6eeae170a-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 47,
              "start": 47
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked whether there were statistics supporting the argument that the purge process was problematic."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "fef6eeae170a58e49c57f7fae6687524d3cc7e589fd23f8b3d1fcdd5892801ff",
            "evidence_ids": [
